 "n30eb8b7d6ad": {
  "row": 10,
  "sub": 7,
  "lines": [
   "7:0.1"
  ],
  "add": "- **Plate settings of the belts:** Circum-Pacific – subduction around the Pacific basin; Mediterranean–Himalayan – continental collision; mid-ocean ridges – divergence; hotspots (Hawaii, Galapagos, Reunion) – mantle plumes under a moving plate."
 },
 "f6e02dddbadf8": {
  "row": 10,
  "sub": 7,
  "lines": [
   "7:0.0"
  ]
 },
 "f7675467920bc": {
  "row": 10,
  "sub": 7,
  "lines": [
   "7:1"
  ],
  "add": "- The Ring of Fire also holds about **75% of the world's active volcanoes**."
 },
 "f9491fc7733eb": {
  "row": 10,
  "sub": 7,
  "lines": [],
  "add": "- **Hotspots** (Hawaii, Galapagos, Reunion): volcanism and quakes over **mantle plumes** beneath a moving plate, away from plate boundaries."
 },
